WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.450
A rising tide of Islamist militancy in Africa
is a growing threat to the US and Europe.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.840
There is a dangerous misconception that African
militant groups are too locally focused or

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.279
weak to pose a real danger.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:22.010
Africa is the next front for the Salafi-jihadi
movement, a global ideological movement that

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.490
includes ISIS and al Qaeda.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:29.779
African Salafi-jihadi groups provide a local
base and source of resilience for these organizations.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:34.050
They are gaining strength not because of ideological
resonance, but because the spread of insurgencies

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.470
and conflict creates opportunities to insinuate
themselves in communities.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:42.440
The Trump administration is trying to do more
against these groups with increased raids

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.600
and drone strikes in places like Somalia.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.780
But it still has failed to recognize the link
between local conflicts and grievances and

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.320
the Salafi-jihadi movement.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:56.470
These local issues—conflict and poor governance—feel
remote and irrelevant to Americans.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:01.440
And the task of resolving them, from Nigeria
to Mali to Libya to Somalia, is large.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.630
But Americans must understand that addressing
these challenges now is far cheaper than fighting

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.000
yet another war.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.920
What's your take on American policy in Africa?

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.660
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.780
Also, let us know what other topics you’d like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:20.580
and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

